    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d187">

                <pb facs="0301" n="227" xml:id="pg227"/>

                <head>Mr. F. W. Seward to Sir F. Bruce</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department Of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-02-21"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 21, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 16th instant, in regard to co-operative measures for
                    securing the suppression of piracy in chinese waters, and, in reply, to inform
                    you that the diplomatic representative of the United States in China, and their
                    chief naval officer, will be instructed to co-operate, so far as they properly
                    can, with those of other western powers, towards the ends indicated in your
                    note.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with high consideration, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>FREDERICK W. SEWARD, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. Sir <hi rendition="#small-caps">Frederick W. A. Bruce</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
